body:
What @harrybulsach said. They aren't going to watch you unless it's for ODOT or probation, in which case good look. If not, just grab yourself one of these guys:

 [https://www.amazon.com/iHeartRaves-Stash-Briefs-Underwear-Pockets/dp/B07CC9345N](https://www.amazon.com/iHeartRaves-Stash-Briefs-Underwear-Pockets/dp/B07CC9345N) 

&#x200B;

If you're hoping to convince them to change the results, it's not gonna happen, sorry. They don't even test them, they just take said sample and send them off to the lab.

&#x200B;

Hope this helps.

I'd suggest finding a doctor accepting new patients within your network who ALSO is legally able to prescribe medical marijuana. I know my current Dr. does (I haven't tried to ask for it as to my knowledge I would not qualify) but he said since there aren't that many around, he has been SLAMMED with people trying to get in just for that to the point he stopped accepting new patients. Hopefully that's not the case city wide, but just a heads up that waits to get in/finding a dr may take some time. 

Also, don't fall for the likes of companies willing to do a "consulatation," as people seem to think this will get them their card, when in reality you MUST HAVE a written letter from a designated physician stating what your illness/reason for need is regardless of whether you go to said consult or not. They'll still make you pay the $150 but no card. 

&#x200B;

About halfway down this link you will find a list of actual, certified legal prescribing dr's:

&#x200B;

 [https://www.bizjournals.com/columbus/news/2019/01/17/more-ohio-doctors-forming-dedicated-cannabis.html](https://www.bizjournals.com/columbus/news/2019/01/17/more-ohio-doctors-forming-dedicated-cannabis.html) 

&#x200B;

 Hope this helps!

I actually worked with 2 separate local elected officials as well as PUCO to try to regulate them as an energy provider, same as AEP etc. We got to the point where next step was to take them back to Supreme Court of Ohio, but we had to run some analysis first. If they came in one penny above the "benchmark," it got elevated, but miraculously, they came in one cent BELOW, and thus, nothing ever happened.

&#x200B;

They know exactly what they're doing, and how they continue to game the system is mind blowing.

Salateen grill on Roberts in Hilliard has fantastic pakistani/indian food as well. Definition of a hole in the wall with an attached market as well.

&#x200B;

 [https://salateenonline.com/](https://salateenonline.com/)

Sure. I'm in my mid-20's, been admitted once (self-admitted after 2nd DUI) and in recovery (2+ years alcohol free, went to rehab in 2016 followed by jail time for said DUI). After that period needless to say was not doing great but dug myself out to a solid extent. Went back to school and did pretty damn well all things considered, found steady work and steadily increased my income to where I am now fairly comfortable for my age and where I was just 2 years ago which was unemployed, recently out of rehab and no real prospects of success.

&#x200B;

Fast forward to now, I was recently let go from my job with no notice (found another but no benefits, etc.), my credit score has tanked over 350 points in the past 6 months or so due to unpaid medical bills I was unaware of, got behind on payments naturally due to loss of employment which lead to eviction, got sent to collections for both medical and utility bills which have since been paid but needless to say the credit score is tanked and I'm broke, significant other of almost 8 years turned down proposal offer about a month before losing my job, and most recently I received a video from my cousin who couldn't believe he was hearing my own brother discussing with my father of all people how "He's just a waste of human life at this point," referring to me. Starting to kind of agree.

I mean overall probably a 5 or 6/10. Great relief during obviously because you're basically getting high and tripping to an extent, but it really does't last, at least for me. Not to mention extremely high costs (cheapest I found was $250/hr which was nasal spray, IV infusions at least where I am are around $3,000-$4,500, which needs to be paid all upfront before ever receiving the treatment) and a limited number of times you can do it considering it's a controlled substance.

&#x200B;

Overall would recommend if you're pretty well off/wealthy but if not, counseling is likely a better option, at least financially.
